Social media ethics are the set of moral principles and guidelines that tell us how to behave responsibly, respectfully and honestly when we use platforms like Instagram, Twitter or TikTok. In your notes they’re broken down into ten key ideas: 

1️⃣ Transparency – always be clear about who you are and what your intentions are;  
2️⃣ Privacy – protect others’ personal information and ask permission before sharing it;  
3️⃣ Respect – avoid harsh, abusive or offensive language;  
4️⃣ Authenticity – be honest, don’t fake followers or reviews;  
5️⃣ Accountability – own up to the consequences of what you post;  
6️⃣ Clarity – make your message unambiguous;  
7️⃣ Brevity – keep it concise;  
8️⃣ Don’t compromise data – don’t exploit user data for profit;  
9️⃣ Unbiased – steer clear of partisan or prejudiced content; and  
🔟 Know your audience – tailor content to their needs while staying ethical.  

Keeping these points in mind helps you build trust and a positive reputation online.
